A new standard-library module, `Std.RealCompleteness`, supplies the completeness of `real`: every nonempty set of reals that is bounded above has a least upper bound. Its one trusted lemma, `Complete`, is an `{:axiom}` lemma that `dafny audit` reports, and it holds of the real numbers, Dafny's model of `real`. Verified from it are `ExistsLub`, `UniqueLub` and a total ghost `Sup` over `iset<real>`, enough to prove, for example, the intermediate value theorem for polynomials of arbitrary degree. A program that does not use the module is unaffected.
